Use the mmap ELF writer only on the build-id path, which never relayouts.

Unconditional ELF_C_RDWR_MMAP (Gentoo bug 980264) leaves section headers stale
when path rewriting shrinks the debug sections and moves e_shoff, breaking strip.

Gentoo bug: https://bugs.gentoo.org/980264
elfutils bug: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=34468

--- a/tools/debugedit.c
+++ b/tools/debugedit.c
@@ -3579,6 +3579,8 @@
 
   if (dest_dir == NULL && (!do_build_id || no_recompute_build_id))
     elf = elf_begin (fd, ELF_C_READ, NULL);
+  else if (dest_dir == NULL)
+    elf = elf_begin (fd, ELF_C_RDWR_MMAP, NULL);
   else
     elf = elf_begin (fd, ELF_C_RDWR, NULL);
   if (elf == NULL)
